\begin{abstract}
Eight supplied 213-state packets are compared at a pinned repository snapshot.
Their ideas are not interchangeable by state number. The selected 197-subtree,
direct-transfer source and its seven-zero origin detector can, however, be
combined with the entry-bypass argument from the earlier 198-subtree machine.
The needed helper is native state 211 rather than 167. Two transition edits
and deletion of native state 112 yield \textbf{212 working states and 424 binary
transitions}. Four universal partial-tape identities prove PA-provable halting
equivalence with the selected U213 parent, preserving its Con(U) endpoint.
The new machine is weakly faster on every common halting run.
This is a conventional mathematical proof with executable checks, not a new
Lean or Rocq endpoint certificate or a global minimality claim.
\end{abstract}

