\begin{abstract}
The three current U211 proposals in ProveIt are distinct machines, including
under state renaming. They implement the same ordered 3,909-primitive source
program, but delete different states from their common U212 parent. Their
patches cannot simply be combined: source reassociation changes the
predecessor bits on which their local proofs depend.

The new argument composes with the retained numerical-calculus and unary
theory U calibration to give the ordinary mathematical, PA-formalizable
endpoint \(\PA\vdash\neg\Halt(U_{209},\mathrm{blank})\leftrightarrow\Con(\PA)\).
This packet supplies no new Lean, Rocq, MM0, or exported PA kernel
certificate. We also prove a separate obstruction: deleting the native
dominated propositional row makes the remaining calculus's consistency
provable in PA, so that apparent simplification loses the desired calibration.
\end{abstract}
